cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this coursework, please cite it as below."
title: "A3-ADL: Multimodal Cancer Classification Challenge 2026 — v10 through v16"
authors:
  - family-names: "Proença"
    given-names: "Rafael"
    affiliation: "Uppsala University"
    email: "rafaeltproenca@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rafallex/A3-ADL"
abstract: >-
  Coursework for the Advanced Deep Learning for Image Processing course
  (1MD042) at Uppsala University, spring 2026. Implements a series of
  iteratively-improved binary classifiers (v10 through v16) for paired
  brightfield + fluorescence microscopy cell images, with a focus on
  out-of-distribution generalization across patients. v16 introduces
  CoMIR-style contrastive self-supervised pretraining, leave-one-patient-out
  cross-validation, EMA-smoothed multi-snapshot ensembling, and an auxiliary
  NT-Xent alignment loss during supervised fine-tuning.
keywords:
  - "deep learning"
  - "multimodal learning"
  - "contrastive learning"
  - "self-supervised learning"
  - "medical imaging"
  - "out-of-distribution generalization"
  - "cancer classification"
  - "microscopy"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-05-15
